Track 1: Azimuth Flutter Bleed
- Story & Context: Julian Ward discovered the corroded lead cylinder lodged beneath the damp timber of the Queen’s Pier excavation, his hands stained with rust as the acrid tang of vinegar syndrome rose from the fractured cassette inside. When he first threaded the ribbon through an overheated Nakamichi deck, a mechanical shudder caused the tape to drag across the playback head, creating an accidental polyrhythmic stammer between a Latin hand drum and a floating choir. As the speed stabilized, Elena’s improvised conga rolls fell into sync with the machine’s flutter, capturing the moment their lead vocalist leaned into the studio ribbon mic to murmur, "The tape unspools into morning light." The studio monitors shook with an impossible, buoyant swing that brought five visiting engineers to an absolute standstill.
